{"availability":"available","full":"paladin-t/my_basic","name":"my_basic","description":"A lightweight BASIC interpreter written in standard C in dual files. Aims to be embeddable, extendable and portable.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C","stars":572,"forks":129,"created":"2014-02-16T09:24:50Z","updated":"2026-08-31T08:09:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"http://paladin-t.github.io/my_basic/","topics":["basic","interpreter","programming-language","scripting-language"],"demo":"https://my-basic.github.io/playground/output/index.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:31.896Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:31.896Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:31.896Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T09:01:31.896Z","stars":572,"forks":129}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["MY-BASIC is a lightweight BASIC interpreter written in standard C in dual files. It aims to be embeddable, extendable and portable. It is a dynamic typed programming language, reserves structured syntax, supports a style of prototype-based programming (OOP), also implements a functional paradigm by lambda abstraction. The core is written in a C source file and an associated header file. It's easy to either use it as a standalone interpreter or embed it with existing projects in C, C++, Java, Objective-C, Swift, C#, etc. and totally customizable by adding your own scripting interface."],"features":["Interpreter workflow diagram"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/paladin-t/my_basic/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"c1ddf40137275450ac4ff00f2771aa30a1628eacfb9428a432ed0f9f85e07e5c","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:31.983Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:31.983Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"MY-BASIC is a lightweight BASIC interpreter written in standard C in dual files. It aims to be embeddable, extendable and portable. It is a dynamic typed programming language, reserves structured syntax, supports a style of prototype-based programming (OOP), also implements a functional paradigm by lambda abstraction. The core is written in a C source file and an associated header file. It's easy to either use it as a standalone interpreter or embed it with existing projects in C, C++, Java, Objective-C, Swift, C#, etc. and totally customizable by adding your own scripting interface.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/paladin-t/my_basic/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"c1ddf40137275450ac4ff00f2771aa30a1628eacfb9428a432ed0f9f85e07e5c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/paladin-t/my_basic/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:31.984Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-31T08:09:15Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/paladin-t/my_basic/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T09:01:31.984Z","hash":"c1ddf40137275450ac4ff00f2771aa30a1628eacfb9428a432ed0f9f85e07e5c","originalBytes":10616,"storedBytes":10616,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["my-basic","basic","core","interpreter","using","module","bas","build","wiki","basic.h","functions","lambda","shell","string","structured","basic.c","binary","diagram","features","file","print","programming","source","standalone","workflow","abstraction","api","collection","customizable","customizing","development","donate","easy","get","installation","introduction","linux","list","main","manipulation","memory","other","output","prototype-based","read","reference","referenced","return","see","setup","usertype","written","about","another","automatic","basic8","both","class","code","compile","data","def","details","donation","enddef","etc.","everything","existing","functional","glance","greeting","hello","how","importing","input","int","integration","lightweight","like","link","linking","load","macos","main.c","multiple","next","overriding","pass","program","projects","quick","real","retro","routine","run","scripting","simple","sta